---
description: Nested selectors that mirror the DOM; structure written again for each layout state
globs: frontend/**/*.{tsx,scss}
alwaysApply: false
---

- Selectors are nested the same way the elements are nested in the DOM.

```scss
.observations-view {
  .observation-filters {
    .filter-field {
      label {
      }
      select {
      }
    }
  }
  .observation-table {
    thead {
      th {
      }
    }
    tbody {
      tr {
        td {
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

- Never use `data-*` attributes for styling. Use classes: `.is-empty`, `.is-active`, `.is-disabled`, `.is-low-sample`.

- When the layout changes by orientation or another state class, the styles are applied in a copy of the same structure, scoped to that state context.

```scss
.observations-view {
  .is-landscape & {
    .observation-filters {
      .filter-field {
      }
    }
    .observation-table {
    }
  }

  .is-portrait & {
    .observation-filters {
      .filter-field {
      }
    }
    .observation-table {
    }
  }
}
```

- One SCSS file per feature folder, imported by the component that owns the root element.
